From ec8bbd39ecbf8cbbf7f73791ddae9760ff48ec2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Franklin <cfranklin4474@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:28:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] mm/tier_ext: replace policies atomically (struct_ops
 .update)

Implement tier_ext_ops .update, so BPF_LINK_UPDATE swaps an attached
policy's programs without detaching: the lruvecs never fall back to the
default in between. The new struct_ops must name the same cgroup and
nodes. Every dispatch site now fetches the callback it uses once
(TE_OP()), since the ops pointer can change while callbacks run; an
RCU grace period after the swap guarantees no old program still runs.

Also drop the lru_add_drain() at the start of victim nomination: folios
in a per-CPU add batch have not been reported to the policy yet, so it
cannot nominate them, and the drain cost every reclaim pass of a policy
that only uses pick_victims to request aging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mm/tier_ext.c | 100 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 mm/vmscan.c   |   7 +++-
 2 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

